  data:  # d0f2
    kind: invariant  # d0f2
    title: "WI-rusil scoping narrows the edge list but not the supported-language set, so any other supported language withholds a project-label claim as 'produced no call edges'"  # d0f2
    status: violated  # d0f2
    priority: 3  # d0f2
    parent:  # d0f2
    tags:  # d0f2
    - taint  # d0f2
    isbefore: []  # d0f2
    duplicate_of: []  # d0f2
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d0f2
    pr_ref:  # d0f2
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-29 while writing INV-pivam's tests.\nWI-rusil scopes the taint blindness check by a claim's DECLARED source languages: _taint_blind_reason filters the EDGE list to the languages a flow can be in (source_languages), but passes the UNSCOPED taint_supported_languages (set(per_lang_sinks)) to compute_boundary_coverage. Every other supported language then has no edges in the scoped list and reads as \"analyzed but produced no call edges\" -- INV-motos' shape (two checks over different populations).\nREPRO (dev, main agent): repo = a.py (`return eval(\"1 + 1\")`) + b.go (os.Getenv, fmt.Println); --taint-sources declaring label build_input for python only; claim build_input must not reach host_fs.\n- python + go: inconclusive rc 2, \"supported language(s) go were analyzed but produced no call edges\".\n- python only: confirmed rc 0.\nDirection: a false INCONCLUSIVE (withholding), not a false clean -- but it makes WI-rusil's scoping inert on any repo with a second supported language.\nFix: scope the supported-language set to source_languages in the same place the edges are scoped."  # d0f2
    fields:  # d0f2
      statement: "When a taint claim's blindness is scoped to the languages its flows can be in, both the edge census and the supported-language set are scoped to that set."  # d0f2
      root_cause: "_taint_blind_reason filters edges by source_languages but passes the unscoped taint_supported_languages to compute_boundary_coverage."  # d0f2
